course: dictionary
lesson: 13860
title: Jumbo and big words
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Jumbo means very large, bigger than usual. You can often work out a new word from the words around it, and that is its context. «We bought a jumbo pack of crayons, with far more crayons than our old box.» The words far more tell you jumbo means very big.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. «We bought a big pack of crayons, with far more crayons than our old box.» The sentence still makes sense, so big is a good match for jumbo, and jumbo is a bigger, stronger word.
explain: Jumbo can also name a very big passenger plane. «The jumbo jet took off from the airport.» A jumbo jet is huge, so the word jumbo is the same idea as before: extra big.
fact: «Jumbo» means very large, bigger than usual.
fact: A jumbo jet is a very big passenger plane, such as the Boeing 747.
fact: Jumbo was a famous huge elephant in the 1800s, shown at London Zoo and in an American circus.
fact: Jumbo can be an adjective, as in «a jumbo pack», or a noun, as in «a jumbo».
fact: You will see jumbo in everyday shopping words such as «jumbo crayons» and «jumbo hot dog».
exercise: «We bought a jumbo pack of crayons.» What does jumbo mean? | *Very large, bigger than usual | Sold in a box only | Coloured bright red | Very small
exercise: «The jumbo jet took off from the airport.» What is a jumbo jet? | *A very big passenger plane | A long, slow train | A kind of boat | A small toy car
exercise: «Jumbo was a famous elephant in London.» Is Jumbo a name here? | *Yes, it is the name of one famous elephant | Yes, it means very small | No, it means a big plane | No, it means a pack of crayons
test: «The shop had jumbo crayons in the window.» What do jumbo crayons look like? | They melt in the sun | They are hard to find | *They are extra big | They are very small
test: «The ___ jet landed safely at night.» Which word fits the gap? | Wooden | *Jumbo | Sleepy | Tiny
exam: Ella says jumbo means small, like a tiny crayon. Is she right? | Yes, jumbo is the same as tiny | No, a jumbo crayon is very big | *No, jumbo means very large, so Ella is wrong | Yes, because a jumbo jet is small
